.TH FMT_TAI 3
.SH NAME
fmt_tai \- format a TAI timestamp as an ISO 8601 string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <fmt.h>
.B #include <tai.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t fmt_tai(char* " dest ", const struct tai* " ta ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fmt_tai
formats the TAI (International Atomic Time) timestamp pointed to by
.I ta
into an ISO 8601 formatted string and writes it to the buffer pointed to by
.IR dest .
.PP
The function extracts the time value from the
.B tai
structure, masks it to ensure compatibility with standard time formats, and delegates the formatting to
.BR fmt_iso8601 (3).
.PP
The resulting string is written to
.I dest
without a null terminator.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes written to the buffer.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fmt_iso8601 (3),
.BR tai (3)